Revert "Reland "Clamp renderer-supplied popup bounds to the display""
(crbugs 578109588, 581335325 and 544041106): the clamp used the popup's
display, but the popup view has no native window yet when ShowPopup()
runs, so <select> popups on a secondary display were clamped to the
primary display's width. Upstream says the int overflow the clamp guarded
against (crbug 544041106) is already mitigated by crrev.com/c/8360076,
and a gated fix is being prepared.
chromium/src main commit da101d1da0d501859d43e4b8b235bc5108e735fa
(main@{#1732805}), merged on 2026-11-04 to the 157 branch
(1edaf78a5e74fb49400629c821d386869c17c8c1, refs/branch-heads/8103@{#1140},
after the 157.0.8103.45 tag). This is the 157 merge without its tests.
Drop it once a 157 tag has it.

diff --git a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_impl.cc b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_widget_host_impl.cc
